{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "The Arithmetic Logic Unit (ALU)", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 12, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 2, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A1.2", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about ALU Arithmetic Logic Unit.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Understand key information about the concepts, principles, and methodologies in simple spoken and written situations.  Read and write about programming techniques, use cases, kinds, and sequences in simple spoken and written situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures.  Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures.", "type": "secondary_1"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le02ob12re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "let's", "type": "name"}, {"content": "we use this expression  to invite someone to do something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(contraction)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: One of the most important parts of the Central Processing Unit is the Arithmetic Logic Unit, let's call it ALU.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le02ob12aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "primary ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "primary means when something is important, when something goes first; rank, importance", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Binary numbers, that's the base 2 number system, and the primary language for computers.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le02ob12aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "CPU", "type": "name"}, {"content": "this is the brain of the computer, this is where the calculations occur", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(acronym)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The CPU processes most of data, so ALU is an important and vital part of data processing.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le02ob12aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "enough ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "sufficient, when there is an amount of something you don't need anymore", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: A good quality processor that transfers the data fast enough.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le02ob12aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "successful ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "high levels of achievement", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You have a good quality processor that transfers the data fast enough in order to make fast and successful transfers.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le02ob12aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "maintenance ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "preserve something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Good maintenance is a key element if you want to keep your CPU clean.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le02ob12aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Look for more information about the ALU system functions. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Design a post whit the origin, definition and functions of the ALU system. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share the poster with your teacher and classmates.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I look for more information about the ALU system functions. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I design a post whit the origin, definition and functions of the ALU system. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share the poster with your teacher and classmates.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Can \u2013 Modal Verb", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<strong>Can</strong> is a very important verb, it's an auxiliary verb and also a modal verb, we use can in several contexts and situations and it's a very helpful verb we can count on.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<strong>Can</strong></br></br>  We use can when we make a reference about <strong>abilities,</strong> we use it to say if we are able to perform an action or not, depending on the possibilities and depending on the circumstances.</br></br>  We use <i>can</i> when we <strong>give permission</strong> or when we <strong>ask for permission, the  verb</strong> <i>can</i> is less formal and more common to use it with friends or an acquaintance, for example.</br></br>  We use can  when we make a <strong>deduction,</strong> when we know something in advance and then we are able to figure out what possibly happens next.</br></br>  <strong>Structure</strong></br></br>  <div class=\"center_text\">Subject + <strong>can</strong> + <strong>main verb in base form</strong> + complement</div></br></br> </br></br> Examples: </br></br><span class=\"italic\">This CPU <strong>can process</strong> information very fast.</span></br><span class=\"italic\"> A good quality processor <strong> can retrieve</strong>  data instantly.</span>   ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "ALU can also perform logic operations with values NOT, AND, OR.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "ALU data processing speed can be fast or slow.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Demonstrative Pronouns", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "We use <strong>the demonstrative pronouns</strong> when we make a reference about two things specifically:</br></br>  <strong>1.Singular or Plural</strong></br> <strong>2. Distance</strong>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<strong>Demonstrative pronouns</strong></br></br>  (This,That,These,Those)</br></br>   When we make a singular sentence with (1 person, 1 object) we use demonstrative pronouns <strong>this</strong> or <strong>that</strong>.</br></br>  <strong>This =</strong> <strong>singular</strong> form and when a person or an object is <strong>near</strong>.</br> <strong>That =</strong> <strong>singular</strong> form and when  a person or an object is <strong>far</strong>.</br></br>  When we make a plural sentence with (+2 persons, +2 objects), we use demonstrative pronouns <strong>these</strong> or <strong>those</strong>.</br></br>  <strong>These =</strong> when <strong>plural</strong>  and when people or objects are <strong>near</strong>.</br> <strong>Those =</strong> when <strong>plural</strong> and when people or objects are <strong>far</strong>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Now you know why computers get hot when working, that's because of ALU. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "That's what you have to do, buy an expensive but effective processor.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"exercises": [{"questions": [], "template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "I can read about ALU.  ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can write sentences correctly about ALU.  ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can understand what ALU is in a written text.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "What kind of pieces make part of the CPU?   ", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": "What's the importance of a circuit in a CPU? ", "type": "Free Header Item"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "We